WEBVTT

00:00:00.103 --> 00:00:05.753
A complete aggregation query has a natural logical
flow First

00:00:05.925 --> 00:00:11.782
FROM identifies the source WHERE filters individual
rows GROUP

00:00:11.796 --> 00:00:16.032
BY forms the groups HAVING removes groups that do
not meet an

00:00:16.046 --> 00:00:20.993
aggregate condition SELECT defines the values that
appear in the result and

00:00:21.019 --> 00:00:26.437
ORDER BY sorts the final rows The written SQL order
is familiar

00:00:26.635 --> 00:00:30.648
but thinking about the logical stages helps explain
why certain expressions are

00:00:30.674 --> 00:00:35.760
valid in one clause and not another There is also a
practical

00:00:35.786 --> 00:00:40.578
efficiency lesson here If a condition can be applied
to individual source

00:00:40.604 --> 00:00:44.039
rows put it in WHERE so fewer rows reach the
grouping stage

00:00:45.767 --> 00:00:49.332
Before running a long summary query read it as a
pipeline source

00:00:49.359 --> 00:00:52.793
rows row filter groups group filter output sort
